What are Central Venous Catheters?
Central Venous Catheters are medical devices consisting of thin, flexible tubes inserted into large veins, typically in the neck, chest, or groin area. These catheters are essential for administering medications, fluids, or nutrients directly into the bloodstream, while also enabling frequent blood draws for monitoring purposes. These devices are critically important for patients requiring long-term intravenous therapies such as chemotherapy, total parenteral nutrition, and hemodialysis.
